<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (However, they don't just fire as the rat physically enters the location. Instead, within a single cycle of a theta wave \(~125 milliseconds\), the hippocampus fires a compressed version of the sequence, representing where the rat was, where it is now, and where it is going.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
282 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 217 0 R
/E (This brings the firing of neurons close enough together in time \(milliseconds\) to trigger Synaptic Plasticity. Without this compression, the brain couldn't "wire" the sequence together because the real-world events are too far apart.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
