<<
/Title (Episodic memory is oriented to the past in a way in which no other kind of memory, or memory system,is. It is the only memory system that allows people to consciously re-experience past experiences. Its special, and unique, relationship to time, surprisingly, is not widely known. Nor is it, I think, adequately appreciated. Most people naturally associate all memory with the past and are astonished to learn that this is not so. -Eden Tulving 2002)
